## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F6 | open | SUGGESTION | .github/workflows/build-macos.yml | 💡 suggestion pair the hosted cli lane s pre warm with the hooks shared cache restore — the established ci yml build mobile yml hosted lane pattern this lane runs on fresh github hosted workspaces macos latest macos 15 intel so every release train re downloads both dylibs live from upstream the pre warm s bounded retries fix the gh 2075 failure class — but the repo s pinned hosted lane pattern test ci sqlite3 hook prewarm guard test dart ac2 ac6 is cache restore pre warm which additionally makes warm runs skip the network entirely yaml name native assets hook cache uses actions cache 55cc8345863c7cc4c66a329aec7e433d2d1c52a9 v6 1 0 with path dart tool hooks runner shared key hooks shared runner os runner arch hashfiles pubspec lock restore keys hooks shared runner os runner arch placed immediately before this step after checkout so hashfiles pubspec lock resolves the committed lockfile on a warm cache the tool reports 0 fetched 1 already verified with zero egress and a brownout window then cannot touch the leg at all — strictly closer to the network independent build goal the pr description states optionally mirror the ci yml hardening timeout minutes 2 continue on error true so a cache service hiccup can never red the leg the self hosted app build lane needs nothing extra — its persistent workdir already carries dart tool hooks runner shared across runs |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

